    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d125">

                <pb facs="0238" n="164" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav01/pg164"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.00/432</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Russia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Francis</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Petrograd</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-07-23T19:00:00+03:31">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 23, 1917, 7 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received July 25, 4.30 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1545. Extreme quiet still prevails here. Minister of Foreign Affairs states
                    Workmen-Soldiers fully recognize Provisional Government ascending [ascendancy]
                    and capital punishment restored in army for desertion, disobedience. Reported
                    Russian losses 50,000 prisoners, many large cannon, because soldiers refused to
                    fight through Bolshevik influence. Such impression greatly weakens
                    Workmen-Soldiers’ influence.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Francis</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
